<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Resto Druids in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Restoration Druid Healer Phase 4</h2>Phase 4 will flip the script once again for how tier gear is acquired. First, you buy tier pieces with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a> to get the ilvl 251 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-843/lasherweave-garb">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Garb</span></a>. Then, you upgrade them with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> from ICC 10H/<wbr/>25N/<wbr/>25H to get the ilvl 264 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-232/sanctified-lasherweave-garb">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lasherweave Garb</span></a>. Then upgrade them once again with the heroic <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> from ICC 25H to get the ilvl 277 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-251/sanctified-lasherweave-garb">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lasherweave Garb</span></a>. Expect to achieve the highest level of tier gear this phase, even as a healer. ICC is one of the raids that people will not stop running for the rest of Wrath, so getting enough <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> is just a matter of time.<br/>
<br/>T10 has the best set bonuses that Resto Druids have seen so far in the expansion. The two piece set bonus: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70658/item-druid-t10-restoration-2p-bonus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Druid T10 Restoration 2P Bonus</span></a> only applies to the base healing of Wild Growth, but is still the best value on a two piece bonus we've gotten, especially with the recent changes to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53251/wild-growth">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_flourish.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wild Growth</span></a> now focusing on targeting players. For the four piece set bonus: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70664/item-druid-t10-restoration-4p-bonus-rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Druid T10 Restoration 4P Bonus (Rejuvenation)</span></a>, probabilistic math suggests that we can expect an extra two <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48441/rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a>s to be rolling across the raid on average from the set bonus (with many variations). This might not sound like a lot, but the strength of these <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48441/rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a>s is a great bonus to healing throughput that maths out greater than the crit bonuses from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67128/item-druid-t9-restoration-4p-bonus-rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Druid T9 Restoration 4P Bonus (Rejuvenation)</span></a>. If those extra <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48441/rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a>s would not be useful, you could now instead roll fewer <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48441/rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a>s for the same coverage and have more bandwidth to use other heals for more targeted impact.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="when-to-swap-to-t10">When to Swap to T10?</h4>T10 can be swapped in as soon as you've acquired four pieces of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=887/lasherweave-garb">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Garb</span></a>, the ilvl 251 T10 set. This includes if you have heroic T9 pieces currently. The boost from the T10 set bonuses makes up the difference in stats between the T9 ilvl 258 pieces and the T10 ilvl 251 pieces.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems-in-phase-4">Gems in Phase 4</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40155/reckless-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Ametrine</span></a> are still greater in value than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40113/runed-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runed Cardinal Ruby</span></a>. As we approach Best in Slot for Phase 4, the totals of haste on gear will be so great that we will get very close to the haste cap of 856 on gear alone. As such, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40113/runed-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runed Cardinal Ruby</span></a>s will eventually fill most gem slots.<br/>
